WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.184 --> 00:00:19.296
"Swallow! Fly away!" the statue yelled. "Fast!"

2
00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:22.990
The statue's stone arm was heading for Swallow.

3
00:00:23.549 --> 00:00:28.962
Then—crack! The other arm broke off too!

4
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:32.440
Swallow was too weak to even lift his head.

5
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.671
Whoosh! The hawk suddenly swooped in.

6
00:00:37.672 --> 00:00:41.962
It grabbed Swallow with its claws and shot upward.

7
00:00:41.963 --> 00:00:46.421
The arms smashed onto the ground.

8
00:00:46.422 --> 00:00:54.308
"Leave Swallow alone!" the statue shouted. "Put him down!"

9
00:00:54.309 --> 00:00:59.504
But the hawk flew in close circles around the statue.

10
00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.820
He clutched Swallow tightly.

11
00:01:03.172 --> 00:01:08.171
"It's all for the best," Swallow said weakly.

12
00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:11.100
"I'm glad I helped you, Prince.

13
00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:15.739
I used to admire beautiful things with all my heart.

14
00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:21.500
But now I know it's better to fill my heart with love.

15
00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.350
Thank you for showing me that."

16
00:01:25.645 --> 00:01:31.671
Swallow's head drooped as the statue's belt crumbled to the ground.

17
00:01:31.672 --> 00:01:36.796
Kee-kee! The hawk let out a happy call.

18
00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:40.980
"You're so cruel!" the statue said.

19
00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:46.560
"I'm crumbling, and my dear friend is dying!"

20
00:01:48.922 --> 00:01:51.879
The hawk gripped Swallow tightly.

21
00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:57.280
"I'm happy because I've waited for this day a long time!"

22
00:01:58.631 --> 00:02:09.046
The statue made a wailing sound. Then—boom!

23
00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:13.200
It crumbled into a pile of stone and dust.

24
00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:18.720
The hawk waited for the air to clear.

25
00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:23.560
Then it gently placed Swallow in a spot of warm sunlight.

26
00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:28.220
The hawk flapped its wings and walked around Swallow.

27
00:02:29.963 --> 00:02:35.087
The sunlight started to shimmer.

28
00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:38.753
Swallow blinked at the bright light.

29
00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.080
His feathers warmed.

30
00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:47.480
Slowly he stood up and stretched his wings.

31
00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:52.400
"I'm not cold anymore," Swallow said.

32
00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:56.840
"And I'm not tired. How is this possible?"

33
00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:02.000
But then he saw the pile of stone and dust.

34
00:03:05.172 --> 00:03:10.421
"Prince!" he cried. "What happened to him?"

35
00:03:10.422 --> 00:03:15.129
"All will be well now," the hawk said.

36
00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:23.414
"But . . . but . . ." Swallow could barely speak. "The statue is gone!"

37
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:30.380
The hawk nodded. "Yes, he is. And it's all thanks to you!"

38
00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:38.140
Swallow felt his heart crack. "You mean I did this to him?"

39
00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:45.440
"No, you did not," the hawk said. "I did."

40
00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:51.760
The hawk flapped its wings once, twice, three times.

41
00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:57.190
Then light swirled into the air.

42
00:03:58.172 --> 00:04:04.129
Poof! The ruined statue disappeared.

43
00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:10.046
Swallow gasped. "What's happening?"

44
00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:14.800
"The spell is finally broken," the hawk said.

45
00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:21.220
Swallow was even more confused. "What spell?"

46
00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:29.470
The hawk dropped its head. "The one I never should have put on him."

47
00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:34.350
"Oh no," Swallow whispered.

48
00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:38.220
"Are you saying that my friend is gone forever?"

49
00:04:38.505 --> 00:04:46.754
"No." A boy stepped out from behind the rosebush.

50
00:04:46.755 --> 00:04:55.832
"Swallow! I am right here!"
